{"name":"Frappé","hex":"#ceae99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frappé","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A frozen fruit-flavoured dessert or appetizer.","Alternative form of frappe (“a liqueur or cocktail served on shaved ice”)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Iced; cooled."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frapp%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frappé coffee","blocks":[{"text":"A frappé coffee, cold coffee, Greek frappé, or just frappé is a Greek iced coffee drink generally made from spray-dried instant coffee, water, sugar, ice and milk. The word is often written frappe. The frappé was invented in 1957 in Thessaloniki through experimentation by Dimitris Vakondios, a Nescafe representative. Greek Christos Lenzos (1930–2023), a coffeehouse (1964–2013) owner in Pangrati, has been recognized for his self-made version of Greek frappé coffee. Frappés are among the most popular forms of coffee in Greece and Cyprus and have become a hallmark of postwar outdoor Greek coffee culture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Cafe-frape-glas-holztisch-unscharf.jpg/330px-Cafe-frape-glas-holztisch-unscharf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frapp%C3%A9_coffee"},{"title":"Milkshake","blocks":[{"text":"A milkshake is a sweet beverage made by blending milk, ice cream, and flavorings or sweeteners such as butterscotch, caramel sauce, chocolate syrup, or fruit syrup into a thick, sweet, cold mixture. It may also be made using a base made from non-dairy products, including plant milks such as almond milk, coconut milk, or soy milk. Dry ingredients such as whole fruit, nuts, seeds, candy, or cookies are sometimes incorporated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Strawberry_milk_shake_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Strawberry_milk_shake_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&ut